1242
01:36:30,320 --> 01:36:37,060
because you can expand and then see the files within it and even scroll through them and see how it changes.

1243
01:36:37,422 --> 01:36:39,076
So this is wonderful.

1244
01:36:39,502 --> 01:36:45,476
But right now, the graph still treats those files mostly as files and connections.

1245
01:36:45,902 --> 01:36:54,308
It doesn't really understand the framework specific roles behind them. So that's what we're adding next framework adapters.

1246
01:36:56,366 --> 01:37:00,032
In this lesson, we'll add framework adapters.

1247
01:37:00,462 --> 01:37:05,636
So head over into specs phase 08 and let's open it up in preview.

1248
01:37:06,510 --> 01:37:12,484
The goal is for our application to recognize what kind of codebase is it looking at.

1249
01:37:13,294 --> 01:37:19,792
An adapter for Next.js will recognize the roles from path conventions and routes derived from those same paths.

1250
01:37:20,032 --> 01:37:29,924
An adapter for Nest.js, for example, will recognize the roles from file name suffixes and routes assembled from decorators on the controller and the method together.

1251
01:37:30,254 --> 01:37:34,244
An adapter for React, which is nearly free once Next.js exists.

1252
01:37:34,926 --> 01:37:36,032
I think you get the idea.

1253
01:37:36,192 --> 01:37:41,540
Some frameworks provide additional meaning to the files that is not present within them.

1254
01:37:42,094 --> 01:37:50,692
And for this build, we'll stay inside of the JavaScript ecosystem, with Next.js, Nest.js, React, and even Express in the next phase.

1255
01:37:51,086 --> 01:37:57,860
But if you want to, the adapter system can be extended later for other frameworks or even other programming languages.

1256
01:37:58,254 --> 01:38:00,292
Moving on to constraints.

1257
01:38:00,878 --> 01:38:04,580
Routes are exact or they're absent.

1258
01:38:04,942 --> 01:38:12,672
Emit a route only when the method and the full pattern are both recoverable from the parse syntax with no inference.

1259
01:38:13,294 --> 01:38:15,712
If either has to be guessed, show nothing.

1260
01:38:15,952 --> 01:38:20,196
Because a wrong route pattern is the same failure as an invented edge.

1261
01:38:20,590 --> 01:38:23,312
This is probably the most important rule in this phase.

1262
01:38:23,502 --> 01:38:27,716
Just like we never invent an edge in the graph, we never guess a route.

1263
01:38:28,110 --> 01:38:32,432
If we can clearly read the method and the full path from the code, we show it.

1264
01:38:32,686 --> 01:38:34,672
But if we can't, we'll leave it out.

1265
01:38:34,832 --> 01:38:41,392
I also want to take a second to talk about the rail taxonomy, which should live apart from the adapters themselves.

1266
01:38:41,710 --> 01:38:49,188
So a browser component can read the list of category names without pulling a parser and a file system library into the bundle.

1267
01:38:49,934 --> 01:38:54,724
And one smaller detail here, the left rail only needs the category names.

1268
01:38:55,118 --> 01:39:00,992
It shouldn't need to load the parser logic just to know it should load controllers, services, and modules.

1269
01:39:01,230 --> 01:39:04,112
So we keep that UI separate from the adapter logic.

1270
01:39:04,352 --> 01:39:05,472
So let's build it.

1271
01:39:05,712 --> 01:39:13,604
Open up a new Claude Code window and tell it to read the ClaudeMD and the phase 8 spec and build it.

1272
01:39:14,030 --> 01:39:16,112
And the phase 8 is built.

1273
01:39:16,462 --> 01:39:19,044
The browser checks are now ours to run.

1274
01:39:19,502 --> 01:39:20,772
So what did it do?

1275
01:39:21,262 --> 01:39:24,964
Each repo is now matched to an adapter in a fixed order.

1276
01:39:25,467 --> 01:39:29,472
Next.js, Nest.js, Docosaurus, React, and then None.

1277
01:39:29,870 --> 01:39:36,548
The adapter gives each file a role, and the rail lists those roles in a fixed order with counts.

1278
01:39:36,878 --> 01:39:40,580
A file with no convention matches goes under unclassified.

1279
01:39:40,878 --> 01:39:43,392
The center column now has a map route switch.

1280
01:39:43,662 --> 01:39:50,112
Clicking a route row selects the file that declares it, and the pane shows each file's role and the real route count.

1281
01:39:50,446 --> 01:39:52,388
