1337
01:44:12,910 --> 01:44:20,580
So in this phase, we're fixing that by adding CommonJ support to the parser and then adding an Express adapter on top of it.

1338
01:44:20,942 --> 01:44:29,776
For that, you can go ahead and open the phase 09, whose only goal is for the code bases that use require to stop drawing empty graphs.

1339
01:44:30,030 --> 01:44:32,260
There are really just two things we're adding here.

1340
01:44:32,878 --> 01:44:39,812
First, we detect the require calls and resolve them using the same resolution logic that we already used for imports.

1341
01:44:40,336 --> 01:44:47,012
Then we can also read what a Comma.js module exports so those files can participate properly in the graph.

1342
01:44:47,662 --> 01:44:50,148
And then we add an express adapter.

1343
01:44:50,670 --> 01:45:00,004
Here, roles come from the folder conventions, so if a file lives in routes, controllers, or services, that helps us understand what that file does.

1344
01:45:00,494 --> 01:45:05,252
And we support both singular and plural folder names because real projects use both.

1345
01:45:06,670 --> 01:45:10,276
