1938
02:35:13,230 --> 02:35:20,708
The tools and the agent itself first, and then the API and its credentials, then the chat panel, and then the evaluation.

1939
02:35:21,038 --> 02:35:29,860
The agent will get six tools a summary of the whole analysis, searching files by part of a path, listing files by role,

1940
02:35:30,256 --> 02:35:35,620
direct neighbors of a file, a transitive walk in either direction, and the route table.

1941
02:35:35,950 --> 02:35:39,972
These tools call the same graph functions that draw the canvas.

1942
02:35:40,334 --> 02:35:42,532
They do not re implement any of it.

1943
02:35:43,950 --> 02:35:45,156
And that part matters.

1944
02:35:45,536 --> 02:35:50,148
The agent shouldn't have its own version of the Blast Radius or dependency traversal.

1945
02:35:50,574 --> 02:35:54,756
It uses the same graph logic that the rest of the application or the trusts.

1946
02:35:55,310 --> 02:36:03,332
But basically, we want to have an agent project that runs as its own service, not inside of the application, built on managed deep agents,

1947
02:36:03,616 --> 02:36:06,276
ran locally, reached over HTTP.

1948
02:36:06,734 --> 02:36:12,016
The runtime provides a server, the threads, and the streaming, so none of these get written by hand.

1949
02:36:12,270 --> 02:36:19,780
Its instructions carry the refusal behavior and the never infer rule, because those are the product's rules rather than the agent's configuration.

1950
02:36:20,238 --> 02:36:26,976
And if you head over to the constraints, you'll see that this constraint is all about credentials.

1951
02:36:27,246 --> 02:36:28,996
It's an important security problem.

1952
02:36:29,776 --> 02:36:34,404
Our agent is reading source code from the repositories that we don't control.

1953
02:36:34,990 --> 02:36:40,548
And source code can contain arbitrary text, even including instructions trying to manipulate the model.

1954
02:36:41,166 --> 02:36:45,316
So we never let the model choose which analysis it has access to.

1955
02:36:45,870 --> 02:36:49,604
That information lives inside a short-lived signed credential.

1956
02:36:50,158 --> 02:36:57,252
The agent can ask the tools questions, but it can't simply switch to another analysis because some source code comment told it to.

1957
02:36:58,382 --> 02:37:02,788
And we also don't give the agent a key that can read every analysis.

1958
02:37:03,118 --> 02:37:08,420
The tools stay scope to the organization and analysis that the conversation belongs to.

